WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.436
-Talk to me about
collaborating with Madonna.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.006
-Oh, my God.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.508
-This was at the
Billboard Music Awards.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.310
You crushed it. It was great.
-Thank you, man.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.844
-And how did you even
rehearse this?

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:13.079
Because it was,
like, holograms of like

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.213
five different Madonnas
or something.

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:15.849
-Wow. That was crazy.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.718
There was like
one week during rehearsals,

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.953
because, actually,
there was the hologram,

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:25.625
so I couldn't see
the Madonnas on the stage.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:29.328
So I had to learn every step
so I could dance with her,

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:32.031
with the four Madonnas
that I had over there.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.867
-But what were you dancing with?
You just had to fake it?

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:36.169
-Yeah, yeah. I had to fake it.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:39.005
That was the tough part,
because I couldn't do, like,

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:42.809
a wrong movement,
because I was going to...

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:45.945
-Yeah. But, I mean, and then
the real Madonna came --

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.480
-And then the real Madonna came,
and I was confused.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.614
No. I'm kidding.

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:50.349
-She's amazing.
-Yeah, she's amazing.

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:51.851
I love her. I love her so much.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:55.588
-Dude, she is so -- I've gotten
to know her through the years,

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:58.625
and she's still, to this day,
very mysterious.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.226
A lot of mystique.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:03.163
-That's the real right word --
very mysterious.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:04.430
-I remember the first time
I met her.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.932
I go, "Oh, my gosh, Madonna."

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.166
I go, "It's an honor
to meet you.

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:11.237
She goes, "Is it?" and left.
Walked away, left.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:14.107
I go, "What did I say?
Did I say something wrong?"

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:17.877
-Well, actually, yeah,
I said that was the right word,

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.413
because when I was
with her in London,

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.415
when we were recording the song
that we have together

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:26.186
that is called "Medellín,"
she was like --

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:28.554
I'm from Medellín, Colombia,
Latino.

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:31.924
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:36.429
So, when I was there in London,
working with her,

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.431
I was in the studio
and I was like,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.500
"What do you think
about these words?

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:46.238
Do you really like it?"
And she was like, "Mm...yeah."

00:01:46.238 --> 00:01:48.707
And I'm like, "That's how
you like it or --"

00:01:48.707 --> 00:01:50.943
-Yeah, like,
"What does that mean?" Yeah?

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:53.947
-And she was like,
"Mm...you can do better,

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:56.849
but If you want to keep that
word, it's okay."

00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:00.153
And I was like, "Wow, okay."
But she's a perfectionist.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:02.555
She loves having
everything on point,

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.890
and that's the great advice
that she gave me once.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.192
So I love her.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.793
And she's Madonna.
She's the queen, man.

00:02:07.793 --> 00:02:10.763
-She's the one-and-only.
She's on this as well, right?

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:15.468
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.669
-"Achepe."
-Yeah, "Achepe."

00:02:17.669 --> 00:02:22.542
-So, I thought the song
originally was called "HP."

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:25.744
I go, "Oh, it's about a printer.
Great."

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:30.349
What is "Achepe?"
Thank you.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:35.021
I was like, "Oh, HP. Cool.
It's a branding thing."

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.822
But, no, "Achepe."

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:39.725
-"Achepe," but you can
name it "HP," too.

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:41.194
-You can.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:44.130
-But, dude, already, it's got
300 million hits on YouTube.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.032
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:50.169
It's a blessing.
It's a blessing.

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:51.637
-Can I just say one thing?

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:54.073
You're the youngest ever to hold
first and second spot

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.709
simultaneously on
the Latin Billboard chart.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.445
That is amazing.
-Yeah, man.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.247
-You have 20 million
YouTube subscribers.

00:03:02.247 --> 00:03:05.317
You have over
42 million Instagram followers.

00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:08.620
Wow!
-Yeah. Thank you.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.990
-And now you're about to drop
this new album on Friday,

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.058
"11:11."

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.093
You're going to go on
a world tour.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.694
-Yeah.
-Are you excited to go on tour?

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:17.763
Do you like going on tour?
-Yeah, I love it.

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:19.064
Actually, I was
missing it a lot,

00:03:19.064 --> 00:03:21.967
because I had a a knee surgery
like six months ago,

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.502
so I had to stop touring.

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:26.438
But now I feel like --

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:28.607
I'm feeling much better,
I feel, after the surgery.

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:30.742
So, yeah, I can't wait
to go to Mexico.

00:03:30.742 --> 00:03:32.544
I'm going to Europe, too.

00:03:32.544 --> 00:03:35.147
Then I'm starting my tour
here in the States

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:38.350
in September and October, so
you guys can't miss it.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.786
It's the 11:11 World Tour.

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:44.423
-A lot of good collaborations
on this album.

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:49.629
Ricky Martin I love.
You have Madonna and Nicky Jam.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:51.064
Is there anyone that you want to

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.732
collaborate with
that you haven't?

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:57.169
-Well, actually, yeah, and I
know you're super-close to him.

00:03:57.169 --> 00:04:00.873
I need your help, man,
in this one.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.408
-Please --
-Don't, don't.

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:03.876
-Yeah.
-No.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:08.881
-Justin Timberlake.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.417
-I can't call him.
-Oh, my God.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.687
-You want me to call him?
-Oh, please.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:15.955
You know what?
Where's my phone.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.223
-Yeah, really.
We'll call him right now.

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.657
-Please, can you call him
from my phone

00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:20.659
so I can save the number,
you know?

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:23.696
-You guys would be great.
You would be fantastic together.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.564
That would just be great.
Justin -- He's watching.

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:30.302
Justin, call Maluma.
This is Gilgigil.

00:04:30.302 --> 00:04:31.704
-Gilgigil?

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.874
-Gilgigil and Maluma has asked
you a favor. Please.

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:37.343
-Yeah, but I don't know if
you're going to be in the song.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:41.146
You want to be in the song?
I'm just kidding.

00:04:41.146 --> 00:04:42.281
-You know -- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:43.616
I know you were playing with
me for a second.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.985
Like, "Does he mean it?"
Like, "Oh."

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.954
You're just mysterious,
like Madonna. Yeah.

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:51.056
You're gonna perform
"HP" tonight.

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:52.258
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:55.360
-Yeah, yeah. "HP."
-Thank you for being here.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.097
Thank you for talking to me.
Maluma, everybody!

